# --- Server-side only (api/parse-homework.js auth) ---
# Firebase Admin SDK credentials, used ONLY by api/_auth.js to verify
# Firebase ID tokens server-side (see comments in that file). This is
# server-only, Node-side config: do NOT prefix these with VITE_ (a VITE_
# prefix tells Vite to bundle a value into the browser build, which would
# leak the private key). Never commit real values or a service-account
# JSON file.
#
# Generate credentials in the Firebase Console: Project Settings -> Service
# Accounts -> Generate new private key. That downloads a JSON file with
# project_id, client_email, and private_key.
#
# Two ways to configure, pick whichever matches where you're running:
#
# 1. Local dev with `vercel dev` (recommended locally): point
#    GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS at the downloaded JSON file's path.
#    api/_auth.js picks this up automatically via applicationDefault().
#    Keep the JSON file outside version control (do not put it in this
#    repo).
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=

# 2. Vercel Preview/Production (no persistent local filesystem to point a
#    path at): copy the three fields from the downloaded JSON into these
#    instead, set as Environment Variables in Vercel (Project -> Settings
#    -> Environment Variables) for Preview/Production, then redeploy.
#    api/_auth.js falls back to these automatically when
#    GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS isn't set.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Gmail OAuth connection (api/gmail-oauth-start.js, api/gmail-oauth-callback.js) ---
# Server-only, used to connect one Gmail account per parent (readonly scope
# only — see api/_googleOAuth.js). Deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_: a
# VITE_ prefix tells Vite to bundle a value into the browser build, which
# would leak the client secret.
#
# Create these in Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials ->
# Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application. Add
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI below to that client's "Authorized redirect
# URIs" list EXACTLY as set here (scheme + host + path, no trailing slash
# difference) — Google rejects any callback whose redirect_uri doesn't
# match one of these exactly.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# e.g. https://your-deployment.vercel.app/api/gmail-oauth-callback
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=
